==========================================
DAY 25 NOTES — Finding Files: find & locate
Date: 23-09-2026
==========================================

WHAT I LEARNED TODAY:
- find searches LIVE through the filesystem — accurate but can be slower
- locate searches a PRE-BUILT DATABASE — nearly instant but can be slightly outdated
- sudo updatedb refreshes locate's database before an important/current search
- find filters: -name, -type (f/d/l), -size (+/-), -mtime (+/-), -empty
- find -exec {} \; runs a command on EACH result — very powerful, also destructive if misused
- ALWAYS run find alone first (without -exec rm) to preview results before deleting anything

COMMANDS I PRACTICED:
[ ] find -name (basic search)
[ ] find -type / -size / -mtime
[ ] find -exec (running a command on results)
[ ] locate (after updatedb)

fill this in after running commands yourself :
$ find ~ -name "notes.txt"
> 

$ find ~ -mtime -1
> 

$ locate notes.txt (after sudo updatedb)
> 


